  "body_text": null,
  "page": null,
  "source": "[\\semigroup]\nDefines: S ::= (X, *)\nextends: S is \\magma via (X, *)\nmeans: * is \\(associative)::binary.operation:on{X}\nEnables:\n. capability: x_ \"in\" S :-> x_ is \\semigroup.element:of{S}\n  written: \"x_? \\in S?\"\nDocumented:\n. called: \"semigroup\"\n. description: \"A semigroup is a magma whose operation is associative, so that\n                $(a * b) * c = a * (b * c)$ for all elements. Associativity\n                makes repeated products unambiguous, so one may write\n                $a * b * c$ without parentheses.\"\nId: \"6ec2faf5-7d2c-4918-a559-6415b94f2b1f\"",
